Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 06:31:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add peer Mesh Links tab for MANET multi-link management

Adds a "Mesh Links" tab to the peer detail page for viewing and editing
the transport links a peer is reachable over (backed by the new
GET/PUT /api/peers/{peerId}/mesh-links endpoint). Multiple links enable
MANET-style multi-path routing with automatic failover.

- MeshLink interface (linkId, transportType, endpoint, mtu, priority,
  cost, wgIfaceName, multicastEnabled).
- PeerMeshLinksSection: fetches the peer's links via useFetchApi, renders
  them in a table, and provides an editor modal to add/edit/remove links
  (with a multicast toggle) that PUTs the set and revalidates.
- Wires the tab into the peer page (gated on peers.read), using the
  existing Tabs, Modal, Button, Input, FancyToggleSwitch and notify
  patterns.

Typechecks clean (tsc --noEmit reports no errors in these files).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
